=== HINT 1: Create shm object ===
int fd = shm_open(SHM_NAME, O_CREAT | O_RDWR, 0600);

=== HINT 2: Set size ===
ftruncate(fd, SHM_SIZE);

=== HINT 3: Map it ===
void *ptr = mmap(NULL, SHM_SIZE, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);

=== HINT 4: Write and read ===
snprintf((char*)ptr, SHM_SIZE, "shared: %d", 42);
printf("shm contents: %s\n", (char*)ptr);

=== HINT 5: Cleanup ===
munmap(ptr, SHM_SIZE);
close(fd);
shm_unlink(SHM_NAME);  // removes the /dev/shm/<name> entry

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
shm_open creates a file in /dev/shm (tmpfs).
MAP_SHARED: writes are visible to all processes that map the same object.
MAP_PRIVATE: copy-on-write, writes not shared.
For synchronization between processes sharing memory: use a semaphore
(sem_open) or a mutex with PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED in the shared region.
Compile with -lrt on older glibc (shm_open/shm_unlink may be in librt).
